select 've-front-of-house', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD 3, 2026-10-31 (Logan). Where BrandDesk stands at the end of 2026-10-31, and what comes next.

1. THE SOCIAL ADD-ON, PHASE 1. BUILT AND PROVEN LIVE, NOT MERGED (branch claude/gifted-cori-ummpqg, commits 8e10876 to 0947fcf). Sean: "Start on the social add-on", then "let's not open social just yet". Setup per client (ve_branddesk_social: two of Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, YouTube, one off Meta; handles; a social manager by sign-in email, never a Guide account; posts a month; Setting up / Running / Paused). Posts (ve_branddesk_social_posts): Draft, sent for the owner's OK, Approved by the owner or on its own 48 hours before its date, Change asked, Posted with each platform's link checked, Skipped. /business/social is the team's planner (clients, a client's month, one post beside their Library); the owner sees Managed by us > Your social. Social at checkout opens by chapter (branddesk.social_chapters, Depot > BrandDesk > Who can sign up > Where social is open) and is EMPTY, so social is closed everywhere but for super admins. Every write to the branddesk setting now merges (saveSettings). ve-branddesk deployed from 1e65808 (version 15, sha256 matched). Proven live on a [TEST] client on Love Life Cafe, then every row removed (ve-once-social-cleanup, now the 410 stub). Defaults (Logan's, Sean's to change): 12 posts a month, the 48-hour OK, the four platforms. Phase 2 not built: social numbers in the monthly report, paying the social manager, a reminder when a post is due, posting through the platforms' APIs.

2. A HANDSHAKE BEFORE THE ASK. LOCKED (canon-ve-front-of-house v8, decision 94a515a4). Free first (their page and the top fixes from their free check, no price), then the $11 Vegan Restaurant Guide, then the BrandDesk pitch page only after a sign or for Sean's warm list. Never a cold $500 ask. Every city stays off until Sean turns it on. To build before outreach: the free check's top fixes in business outreach's first email, and a Signs filter on the pitch list.

3. STATUS. Built: the sample site and make-it-yours switch, Managed by us and Have us do it, the agreement and Stripe (live, checkout open only to super admins until Sean opens a listing), onboarding with the website archive, Library and asset sheet, brand kits, the photographer shot list, the pitch list and pitch pages, visit bounties, the monthly check-in and report, the rotation, social phase 1. NOT built: the website launch (the real client site), the two handshake builds, a Community Manager's view and pay, payouts (Stripe Connect), the premium listing, the Guide's BrandDesk demo tab, social phase 2, the ad console. Sean also named Community Manager recruiting in every chapter (deferred: "let's not stray too far").

4. NEXT: THE WEBSITE LAUNCH (Sean: "we're going to go ahead with the website launch"). Each client's site is built from their Cartridge on the same frame as business/site.html; it goes up on a preview address for the owner's approval; then it moves to their own domain with SSL and a final check of every page; one shared hosting project serves every client site. Then the handshake builds, then outreach to the chapters with the biggest gaps and most signs, once Sean confirms everything is buttoned up.

Open for Sean: merge the branch, which chapters open social, the first real pitches, the BrandDesk trademark and domain check.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
